{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["And now he calls himself <b>who hears the words of El</b> and <b>who sees the vision of Shaddai</b>, as he did in the third prophecy, and he further calls himself <b>who knows the knowledge of Elyon</b>. Now, one who says, \"I know the knowledge of so-and-so,\" means that he recognizes from him what is in his heart — things that he will not express with his mouth. So too here, the intent is to say that he knows and will now declare what is in the mind of El Elyon to do in His world at the end of all days. This is like the matter that is said: \"For a day of vengeance is in My heart\" (Isaiah 63:4), and they said (Ecclesiastes Rabbah 12:10): the heart is not revealed through the mouth. Now, the verse says here, \"he took up his parable and said,\" and it did not mention that this was in prophecy as it mentioned on the three previous occasions, for since he said, \"the utterance of who hears the words of El\" and \"who sees the vision of Shaddai,\" it is known that the hand of HaShem was upon him as in the third time, when it says, \"and the spirit of Elohim came upon him\" (Numbers 24:2), and he called himself thus:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:08:25.769831003Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}